k that link just yet because the  sony news doesn't stop there as a part  of the refresh ps plus ubisoft plus  classics is being bundled into the  playstation plus extra and premium tiers  ubisoft plus classics will launch with  27 curated games on june 30th in the us  and the lineup is expected to grow to  around 50 games by the end of the year  the initial list includes ac valhalla  for honor and a few trials games the  standard version of ubisoft plus will be  added to playstation at a later date the  service will also be coming to xbox in  the future and more of its games will be  available through game pass as a part of  a new deal between the companies so now  that you have this large preview of what  the new ps plus will look like are you  sold let me know in the comments and  while sony was dropping a list of games  warner brothers was busy revealing new  characters for its upcoming free-to-play  platform fighter multiverses a new  cinematic trailer shows a few characters  we've already seen being forced to team  up including batman and shaggy bugs  bunny and arya stark garnett from steven  universe and jake from adventure time  harley quinn also makes an appearance  but her teammate is the trailer's first  confirmed new character the tasmanian  devil from looney tunes the end of the  trailer also teases two more new  additions to the roster velma from  scooby-doo and the iron giant from the  1999 film before confirming an open beta  test is coming in july more details on  the closed alpha test scheduled for may  19th through the 27th were also unveiled  as the test will feature 15 characters  including taz and velma as well as seven  maps ranging from the bat cave to the  haunted mansion from scooby-doo the test  will feature multiple game modes  including 2v2 1v1 4 player free for all  and a training mode hit the comment  section and let me know who you're  planning to main in multiverses and i'll  see you tomorrow  you
 

